  "findings": [
    "The sketch child base constructor obtains its backend through the active factory virtual slot 0x28; its current pointer and factory vtable agree with the static initializer.",
    "Selected spline construction uses a temporary adjacent-point filter with strict squared-distance greater than 1e-8, while preserving the original input record container separately.",
    "Builder dispatch distinguishes two points, three points, larger open/closed inputs and tangent-related options; these are not one generic interpolation call.",
    "A conditional record export uses BRepAdaptor_Curve::BSpline, then Geom_BSplineCurve::Knots. It evaluates mapped knot parameters through the curve virtual evaluator and emits XYZ plus each parameter.",
    "The knot map subtracts the first knot, multiplies by the reciprocal knot span, multiplies by the curve parameter span, then adds the first parameter. Native MINSD applies an upper-parameter comparison before evaluation. No lower clamp was observed in this helper.",
    "Source records, control records, temporary filtered records and derived display subdivisions remain distinct. A universal substitution with poles, mesh/display points or knot samples would change some native paths."
  ],
  "applicationGap": {
    "currentModel": "Sketch v1 has point records, separate segment and arc arrays, constraints and an optional rigid UV frame; no spline record carrier or common ordered child collection.",
